{
  "file": "crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs",
  "item": "fn[agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets]/impl[GraphWithChangingEdges/Fingerprinting]/fn[fingerprint]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "Fingerprinting is required by validation, but this regression\n observes only the outgoing-edge selection. No node contents\n are read, so producing a content fingerprint would violate the\n asserted selection-only dependencies."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `fingerprint` in `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs#fn[agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets]/impl[GraphWithChangingEdges/Fingerprinting]/fn[fingerprint]` is acceptable.\n\n- **Form:** The citation is a fenced commentary block on an explicit function with a body. That is a permitted form for the built-in.\n- **Substance:** The reason is not just that the code is hard to cover. The function is a deliberate `panic!` guard. The `Fingerprinting` trait requires it, but the test is meant to prove that edge inspection never reads or fingerprints node contents.\n- **Agreement with the source:** The test asserts that the recorded dependencies are only `Dependency::OutgoingEdges(1, (), edge_fingerprint(&graph, &[2]))`. `edge_fingerprint` in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/graph.rs` hashes only node paths from `node_path`. It never calls `Fingerprinting::fingerprint`. `node_content` is also a panic guard, and `load_evidence` returns `None`. So no content fingerprint belongs in this scenario, and the function is correctly never executed.\n- **Other uses:** Other tests cover content fingerprints, so the exception does not hide missing coverage of required behavior.",
